  "holistic_F_N": 2,
  "holistic_F_H": -2,
  "section_notes": "S1 is strict: all thermal incidents reported within 24 hours, fuller reports within 30 days, and customer notice within 72 hours. S2 sets a 55°C test and a 5% corrective-action benchmark but does not stop sales above it, while requiring per-model numeric results to customers but not public publication. S3 requires new-unit shut-off within 12 months and retrofit within 6 years with a feasibility escape. S4 requires built-in fire suppression after 36 months. S5 mandates recall at 8/100k after validation with 72-hour customer notice, but serious-injury recall is discretionary."
 },
